-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  std_libc_c.adam - System.LibC.C: every routine it declares, called once
  from libc.a (res/libs/vendor/<triple>, musl's math built by AdamLang-Libs)

  Each routine runs on an input whose result is known: exact ones compared
  exactly (ceil, fma, the l / ll roundings, ilogb, nextafter), the others
  within 1e-12 of the value (float32 forms within 1e-5), the Bessel values
  from mpmath at 30 digits. The out parameters (frexp's exponent, modf's
  integer part, remquo's quotient bits, lgamma_r's sign) are checked too,
  and the constants against the routines (M_PI = 4 atan(1)). A row whose
  name the build cannot bind fails the link, so the row also proves each
  name is in the archive. Each row prints ok or FAIL with its name.
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind run
  exitcode 0
